<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<tmc-service-inc>
<pub id="RM0550J">
<servcat id="08">
<name>Heater &amp; Air Conditioner/Ventilation</name>
<section id="1002K_S000B" variety="S000B">
<name>Air Conditioner</name>
<ttl id="1002K_S000B_7422B_T002L" variety="T002L">
<name>Air Conditioner Tube &amp; Accessory Assembly</name>
<para id="RM0000007R600EX" category="G" type-id="8000T" name-id="52282-00" from="200612">
<name>On-vehicle Inspection</name>
<subpara id="RM0000007R600EX_01" type-id="01" category="01">
<s-1 id="RM0000007R600EX_01_0001" proc-id="RM0550J___000016K00000">
<ptxt>Inspect Air Conditioner Tube &amp; Accessory Assembly</ptxt>
<content1 releasenbr="1">
<s2>
<ptxt>Inspect vehicle wire harness</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Disconnect the pressure sensor connector.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the resistance of the vehicle side wire harness connector terminal of the pressure sensor.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E103262J01" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Resistance:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.94in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.16in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>1 (-) - Body ground</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Always</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Below 1 Ω</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the terminals of the vehicle side wire harness connector of the pressure sensor.</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E103262J02" width="2.775699831in" height="1.771723296in"/>
</figure>
<table>
<title>Voltage:</title>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.97in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.03in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.13in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>3(+) - 1(-)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>IG ON</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4.5 to 5.5V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</s3>
</s2>
<s2>
<ptxt>Inspect pressure sensor</ptxt>
<s3>
<ptxt>Install the air conditioner tool set.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Connect the pressure sensor connector.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Start the engine and operate the air conditioner.</ptxt>
</s3>
<s3>
<ptxt>Using SST (Toyota electrical tester), measure the voltage between the connector terminals of the air conditioner amplifier assembly. (see <xref label="Seep01" href="RM0000005KW01EX"/> for Terminals of ECU)</ptxt>
<sst>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09082-00030</s-number>
</sstitem>
<sstitem>
<s-number>09083-00170</s-number>
</sstitem>
</sst>
<figure>
<graphic graphicname="E132834J01" width="2.775699831in" height="3.779676365in"/>
</figure>
<spec>
<title>Voltage</title>
<table>
<tgroup cols="3" align="center">
<colspec colname="COL1" colwidth="1.17in"/>
<colspec colname="COL2" colwidth="1.79in"/>
<colspec colname="COL3" colwidth="1.17in"/>
<thead>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Tester Connection (Terminal Symbol)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Condition</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Standard</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</thead>
<tbody>
<row>
<entry morerows="2" valign="middle">
<ptxt>A9(PRE) - A13(SG-2)</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>Normal</ptxt>
<ptxt>0.196MPa{2.0kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>}-3.14MPa{32.0kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>}</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0.76 to 4.74V</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>When Malfunctioning</ptxt>
<ptxt>0.196MPa{2.0kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>Below }</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>0.76V or less</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
<row>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>When Malfunctioning</ptxt>
<ptxt>3.14MPa{32.0kgf/cm<sup>2</sup>} or more</ptxt>
</entry>
<entry valign="middle">
<ptxt>4.74V or more</ptxt>
</entry>
</row>
</tbody>
</tgroup>
</table>
</spec>
<atten4>
<ptxt>The pressure sensor connector is a waterproof connector, so perform the inspection on the air conditioner amplifier assembly side. If the measured value is 1V or less, an open circuit in the wire harness is also possible.</ptxt>
</atten4>
</s3>
</s2>
</content1>
</s-1>
</subpara>
</para>
</ttl>
</section>
</servcat>
</pub>
</tmc-service-inc>